note probe: `elif COND` is not a keyword. It compiles as an assignment to a new local named elif, and the
note line after it runs whenever the if arm runs. With x = 1 an elif chain would return 1; this returns 2.
fn main to int
x = ulong 1
r = int 0
if lt x 2
r = int 1
elif lt x 5
r = int 2
else
r = int 3
end
ret r
end
